        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-10T06:41:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ever since I first played against Kaargra, I've wanted to use the title deck in games against other villains.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My idea is to take the Title deck, Crowd's Favor, and Bloodsworn Collesium and play them as a fourth deck against other villains. &nbsp;The titles would play as normal, and you'd collect favor as normal, but instead of 20 favor being an alternate win/lose condition, increasing favor would just be generally beneficial. &nbsp;My current idea is that every 10 favor would grant whichever side has the favor a global +1 to damage.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thematically, Kaargra has replaced her regular gladiators with a special contest: the heroes versus whichever villain you're fighting.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>What do you think?</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:43:42.144Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
